#, no-c-format
msgid "W*"
msgstr "Wind"

#, no-c-format
msgid "Average dry thermal updraft strength near mid-BL height. Subtract glider descent rate to get average vario reading for cloudless thermals. Updraft strengths will be stronger than this forecast if convective clouds are present, since cloud condensation adds buoyancy aloft (i.e. this neglects \"cloudsuck\"). W* depends upon both the surface heating and the BL depth."
msgstr "Prosjekna snaga vjetra u termikama na srednjoj visini BL-a. Oduzmi opadajuci brzinu jedrilice da bi se dobio prosječni čitomer za oblačne termike. Snage vjetra će biti veće od ove prognoze ako postoji konvektivna oblaka, jer se vodeni sploštenje u visini dodjeljuje (tj. to zanemaruje \"oblaksuck\")."

#, no-c-format
msgid "BL Wind spd"
msgstr "Brzina BL-a"

#, no-c-format
msgid "The speed and direction of the vector-averaged wind in the BL. This prediction can be misleading if there is a large change in wind direction through the BL."
msgstr "Brzina i smjer vektorskih srednjepoloženih vjetra u BL-u. Ova prognoza može biti loša ukoliko postoji velika promjena smjera vjetra kroz BL."

#, no-c-format
msgid "H bl"
msgstr "H bl - Hr bl"

#, no-c-format
msgid "Height of the top of the mixing layer, which for thermal convection is the average top of a dry thermal. Over flat terrain, maximum thermalling heights will be lower due to the glider descent rate and other factors. In the presence of clouds (which release additional buoyancy aloft, creating \"cloudsuck\") the updraft top will be above this forecast, but the maximum thermalling height will then be limited by the cloud base. Further, when the mixing results from shear turbulence rather than thermal mixing this parameter is not useful for glider flying."
msgstr "Visina vrha mješavinske slojeve, koja za konvektivne termike predstavlja prosječnu vrhu slobodnog vjetra. Na ravnom području maksimalne visine termikiranja će biti niža zbog opadajuce brzine jedrilice i drugih faktora. U prisutnosti oblaka (koji uvis emitiraju dodatno vodeno sploštenje, stvarajući \"oblaksuck\") vrh upada će biti iznad ove prognoze, ali maksimalna visina termikiranjaće se ograničiti na podoložbu oblaka. Navedena je za \"slobodne\" termike, parametar zanemaruje učinak \"oblaksuck\"."

#, no-c-format
msgid "dwcrit"
msgstr "dwcrit - dubinska kritična visina"

#, no-c-format
msgid "bl cloud"
msgstr "bl oblaci"

#, no-c-format
msgid "This parameter provides an additional means of evaluating the formation of clouds within the BL and might be used either in conjunction with or instead of the other cloud prediction parameters. It assumes a very simple relationship between cloud cover percentage and the maximum relative humidity within the BL. The cloud base height is not predicted, but is expected to be below the BL Top height."
msgstr "Ovaj parametar pruža dodatnu metodu procjene formiranja oblaka u BL-u i može se koristiti zajedno s ili umjesto drugih predviđaja o oblaku. Pretpostavlja vrlo jednostavnu odnosnog između procentne stope pokrivenosti oblakom i maksimalne relativne vlaznosti u BL-u. Visina podoložbe oblaka nije prognozirana, ali se očekuje da će biti ispod visine vrha BL-a."

#, no-c-format
msgid "Sfc temp"
msgstr "Sfc temp - povrsinski temperature"

#, no-c-format
msgid "The temperature at a height of 2m above ground level. This can be compared to observed surface temperatures as an indication of model simulation accuracy; e.g. if observed surface temperatures are significantly below those forecast, then soaring conditions will be poorer than forecast."
msgstr "Temperatura na visini 2m iznad zemlje. Može se uspoređivati s observiranim temperaturem podloge kao indikator modelne simulacije točnosti; npr. ako su observirane temperature podloge znatno niži od prognoziranih, onda će jezgarno stanje biti gorsko nego prognozirano."

